# tests/hello, as an ENTRY (design/caos-expr.md, Phase 3): evaluating this
# directory yields the test's ARG TREE, which dev/run-test then runs.
#
# A CLIENT TEST — it drives `caos-cli` and asserts on what the CLIENT resolves,
# so its base is `DEEP-DEPS/lib` (tests/lib), the image that stages a git
# worktree and then runs `worker1`. DEPping on `lib` is the honest, greppable
# marker of which tests are client tests; most are not, and name std/bash.
#
#   --test  this directory itself, staged into the repo as ./test with its
#           DEEP-DEPS alongside. `--test:@=.` is inert by construction:
#           `strip_caos_expr` removes this file from the tree before the
#           expression is evaluated against it, so nothing recurses.
#   --cli   the client under test; --salt is what makes --test-salt re-run this
curry --base:@=DEEP-DEPS/lib --worker1:@=worker.sh --test:@=. --cli:@=cli --test-salt:@=test-salt
